# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is the template.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the client, and it inlines
# them into the built bundle at build time. Everything here is therefore PUBLIC —
# never put a secret in this file or in .env.
#
# For GitHub Pages, these must also exist in the CI environment, since the bundle
# is built there. Add them under:
#   Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Variables
# and reference them in .github/workflows/deploy.yml, e.g.
#   env:
#     VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY: ${{ vars.VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY }}
# Use "Variables", not "Secrets" — these are not secret, and Actions masks
# secrets in logs which makes build issues harder to debug.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Firebase — powers the "N people viewing now" presence counter ────────────
#
# Get these from the Firebase console:
#   Project settings → General → Your apps → SDK setup and configuration → Config
#
# The presence widget uses Realtime Database ONLY. Firestore is not used and is
# not a substitute: it has no server-side onDisconnect, so a closed tab would
# never clear. If you create the project fresh, add a Realtime Database (not just
# Firestore) or VITE_FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL will not exist.
#
# The Firebase web API key is an identifier, not a credential — it is designed to
# ship publicly. Access control comes entirely from Database Rules, so set them:
#
#   {
#     "rules": {
#       "presence": {
#         ".read": true,
#         "$conn": {
#           ".write": "!data.exists() || !newData.exists()",
#           ".validate": "newData.hasChildren(['at']) && newData.child('at').isNumber()"
#         }
#       }
#     }
#   }
#
# Leave every value below blank and the counter simply stays hidden — the site
# builds and runs fine without Firebase. Presence is strictly optional.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project.appspot.com
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# Must be the Realtime Database URL, NOT the Firestore one. Region-dependent:
#   https://your-project-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com              (us-central1)
#   https://your-project-default-rtdb.asia-southeast1.firebasedatabase.app
VITE_FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL=

# storageBucket and messagingSenderId appear in the console's config block but
# are not needed for Realtime Database — omitted deliberately.
